Jonathan “Benjo” Manigo is a Filipino visual artist with over two decades of experience dedicated to the arts. Born November 8, 1973, he is known for versatility across portraits, landscapes, seascapes, floral, still life, animals, Christian themes, rural scenes, abstracts, cubism, surrealism, and murals.

## Exhibitions and collections

His work has been shown at Festival Mall and Alabang Town Center in Muntinlupa City, and is held in private collections in Makati. He joined the Muntinlupa Art Society in 2000 and has remained active in art groups across the Philippines, refining his craft in varied studio and community settings.

## Background

Jonathan studied at MATS College of Technology in Davao City, moved to Manila in 1995, and made oil his primary medium by 1998 after apprenticing at a Manila gallery. He works in oil across animals, Christian themes, and rural scenes as well as the genres above.

## This gallery

The paintings on this site are original oils organized by genre on the Work page. For a custom piece, use the commission inquiry form — Jon reviews every message and connects you with Benjo for pricing and agreement.
